  "intro": "<p>These are names Victorian families actually used. There are no official rankings for Queen Victoria's reign (1837–1901), so we used the closest reliable evidence: the Office for National Statistics top 100 for babies born in 1904, the earliest official list, plus Douglas Galbi's study of name frequencies in England and Wales through the 1800s. Every name here was in the ONS 1904 top 100, and the note says where.</p><p>Meanings come from Behind the Name. Many Victorian favourites were revivals of medieval or Old English names, and a few, like Ethel and Daisy, were brand new in the 1800s.</p>",
